Hey @mchandschuh - the `OandaFillsForwardDailyForexOnWeekends` test is failing with the latest commit. There are now 5 bars emitted from the FFE. The 5 bars emitted are:

| Bar.Time | Bar.EndTime |
| --- | --- |
{7/19/2012 8:00:00 PM} | {7/20/2012 8:00:00 PM}
{7/19/2012 4:00:00 AM} | {7/20/2012 4:00:00 AM} 
{7/20/2012 12:00:00 AM} | {7/21/2012 12:00:00 AM}
{7/21/2012 8:00:00 PM} | {7/22/2012 8:00:00 PM}
{7/22/2012 8:00:00 PM} | {7/23/2012 8:00:00 PM}

The second bar looks freaky - it's before the first. Stepping through the test, I notice that when the test first gets to `RequiresFillForwardData()`, the `nextFillForwardTime` is calculated correctly. However, when the `fillForward.Time` is calculated you use `RoundDownInTimeZone`. Correct me if I'm wrong, but I think it would be incorrect to calculate the `fillForward.Time` in the data tz because the fill forward frontier time is based on the exchange Tz not the data Tz, i.e.

```
// find the next fill forward time after the next market open
 var nextFillForwardTime = Exchange.Hours.GetNextMarketOpen(previous.EndTime, _isExtendedMarketHours) + fillForwardResolution;
```

In other words, I think we should swap `RoundDownInTimeZone` for `RoundDown` one line 277 of the FFE.

issue_context.body:
For the algorithm below, the enumerator used for the Oanda EURUSD subscription is the `FillForwardEnumerator`.
```
 public class BasicTemplateAlgorithm : QCAlgorithm
    {
        private Symbol _symbol;
        private DateTime _previous;
        private SimpleMovingAverage _sma;

        public override void Initialize()
        {
            HistoryProvider = null;
            SetStartDate(2012, 7, 20);
            SetEndDate(2012, 7, 26);
            _symbol = AddForex("EURUSD", Resolution.Daily, Market.Oanda).Symbol;
            _sma = SMA(_symbol, 5, Resolution.Daily);
            SetBenchmark(date => 0);
        }

        public override void OnData(Slice data)
        {
            if (_previous.Date == Time.Date) return;

            Log(Time.Date.ToString("yyyyMMdd") + ": " + Securities[_symbol].Close + " " + _sma);
            _previous = Time;
        }
    }
```

In the algorithm above, the SMA indicator is never updated.The following table lists the first four bars emitted by the FillForwardEnumerator for the above algorithm:

| BaseData Emitted By FFE  | BaseData.Time | BaseData.EndTime |
| ------------- | ------------- | ------------- |
| 1 | Thursday 7/19/2012 8:00:00 PM  | Friday 7/20/2012 8:00:00 PM |
| 2  | Friday 7/20/2012 12:00:00 AM  | Saturday 7/21/2012 12:00:00 AM  |
| 3  | Saturday 7/21/2012 8:00:00 PM  | Sunday 7/22/2012 8:00:00 PM  |
| 4  | Sunday 7/22/2012 8:00:00 PM  | Monday 7/23/2012 8:00:00 PM |

The result of this `FillForwardEnumerator` is is that 8 hours of precision are lost when the second bar is emitted.

The following test can reproduce the issue above:

```
        [Test]
        public void OandaFillsForwardDailyForexOnWeekends()
        {
            var dailyBarsEmitted = 0;
            var fillForwardBars = new List<BaseData>();

            // 3 QuoteBars as they would be read from the EURUSD oanda daily file by QuoteBar.Reader()
            // The conversion from dataTimeZone to exchangeTimeZone has been done by hand
            var data = new BaseData[]
            {
                // fri 7/20
                new QuoteBar{Value = 0, Time =  new DateTime(2012, 7, 19, 20, 0, 0), Period = Time.OneDay},
                // sunday 7/22
                new QuoteBar{Value = 1, Time = new DateTime(2012, 7, 21, 20, 0, 0), Period = Time.OneDay},
                // monday 7/23
                new QuoteBar{Value = 2, Time = new DateTime(2012, 7, 22, 20, 0, 0), Period = Time.OneDay},
            }.ToList();
            var enumerator = data.GetEnumerator();

            var market = Market.Oanda;
            var symbol = Symbol.Create("EURUSD", SecurityType.Forex, market);

            var marketHours = MarketHoursDatabase.FromDataFolder();
            var dataTimeZone = marketHours.GetDataTimeZone(market, symbol, SecurityType.Forex);
            var exchange = new ForexExchange(MarketHoursDatabase.FromDataFolder().GetExchangeHours(market, symbol, SecurityType.Forex, dataTimeZone));

            var fillForwardEnumerator = new FillForwardEnumerator(enumerator, exchange, Ref.Create(TimeSpan.FromDays(1)), false, data.Last().EndTime, Time.OneDay);

            while (fillForwardEnumerator.MoveNext())
            {
                fillForwardBars.Add(fillForwardEnumerator.Current);
                Console.WriteLine(fillForwardEnumerator.Current.Time.DayOfWeek + " " + fillForwardEnumerator.Current.Time + " - " + fillForwardEnumerator.Current.EndTime.DayOfWeek + " " + fillForwardEnumerator.Current.EndTime);
                dailyBarsEmitted++;
            }

            Assert.AreEqual(dailyBarsEmitted, 3);
            Assert.AreEqual(fillForwardBars[0].Time, new DateTime(2012, 7, 19, 20, 0, 0));
            Assert.AreEqual(fillForwardBars[1].Time, new DateTime(2012, 7, 22, 20, 0 , 0));
            Assert.AreEqual(fillForwardBars[2].Time, new DateTime(2012, 7, 23, 20, 0, 0));
        }
```

The Assert statements in the above test list what I *think* the `BaseData` objects emitted from the `FillForwardEnumerator` should look like. I'm still a slightly hazy on what happens to the first hour the Oanda exchange is open on Sunday (7:00PM to 8:00PM EST).
